5:What is the difference between Evaluation Criteria:
created
created and every time edited
created and edited to meet criteria?

1. CREATED

The rule is evaluated only when the record is created.

Example criteria:

Lead.Status = 'New'

If the Lead is created with Status = New → Workflow runs.

If you later edit the Lead → it does not run again.

2. Created and every time it's edited

The rule is evaluated:

When the record is created
Every time the record is edited

provided the criteria are true.

Example:

Account.Rating = 'Hot'

Account is created as Hot → ✅ runs.

Later you change Phone → Rating is still Hot → ✅ runs again.

Later you change Industry → Rating is still Hot → ✅ runs again.

3. Created and edited to meet criteria

This is the one interviewers usually test.

The Workflow runs when the record changes from NOT meeting the criteria → meeting the criteria.

Example:

Opportunity.StageName = 'Closed Won'

Timeline:

Created as Prospecting
        ↓
No workflow

Changed to Proposal
        ↓
No workflow

Changed to Closed Won
        ↓
✅ Workflow runs

Amount changed
while still Closed Won
        ↓
❌ Doesn't run again

